# Cloudflare Pages custom headers.
#
# NOTE (verified 2026-10-10): this file works on the pages.dev domain but is
# OVERRIDDEN on the docotia.com custom domain by a zone-level Cache Rule
# (Cache Rules > Browser Cache TTL), which forces
# 'cache-control: public, max-age=14400' onto every static asset. So do not
# rely on this file alone for the custom domain — see the ?v= query-string
# versioning on style.css in each page's <head>, which is the fix that
# actually works on docotia.com. To make this file effective on the custom
# domain, the zone Cache Rule's Browser Cache TTL must be set to
# "Respect Existing Headers" in the Cloudflare dashboard.
#
# Background: style.css defaulted to a 4-hour browser cache. On a site edited
# frequently that means a visitor can keep rendering a stale stylesheet for
# hours after a deploy — new HTML arrives but the old CSS is still applied, so
# layout changes appear not to have shipped. Keep this file in the repo root
# (Cloudflare Pages reads it at deploy time).

/style.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
